From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: redwhisk <254472559+redwhisk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:49:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] target/arm: Add a 'dic' property to -cpu max

In system emulation -cpu max reports CTR_EL0.DIC, so a guest never
issues IC IVAU, and the previous patch cannot help it when another
process writes its RAM. Add a 'dic' property, so that a user of such a
setup (vhost-user back-ends with a shared memory backend) can ask the
guest to perform the maintenance with dic=off. CTR_EL0.IDC is left as
it is: data cache maintenance has no effect on translations.

Signed-off-by: redwhisk <254472559+redwhisk@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
---
 docs/system/arm/cpu-features.rst | 11 +++++++++++
 target/arm/tcg/cpu64.c           | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/cpu-features.rst b/docs/system/arm/cpu-features.rst
index 024119449..8f84ac4ef 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/cpu-features.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/cpu-features.rst
@@ -228,6 +228,17 @@ and QARMA3 algorithms have good cryptographic properties, but can
 be quite slow to emulate.  The impdef algorithm used by QEMU is
 non-cryptographic but significantly faster.
 
+``dic``
+  Report ``CTR_EL0.DIC``, which tells the guest that it does not need to
+  invalidate the instruction cache (``IC IVAU``) to make written data
+  visible to instruction fetches.  Enabled by default for ``-cpu max`` in
+  system emulation.
+  QEMU already drops its translations of memory that the guest CPU or a
+  QEMU device writes, but not of memory written by another process that
+  shares guest RAM, such as a vhost-user back-end using a shared memory
+  backend.  Use ``dic=off`` in that case, so that the guest's ``IC IVAU``
+  drops the stale translations.
+
 SVE CPU Properties
 ==================
 
diff --git a/target/arm/tcg/cpu64.c b/target/arm/tcg/cpu64.c
index 687195638..9e1f2c371 100644
--- a/target/arm/tcg/cpu64.c
+++ b/target/arm/tcg/cpu64.c
@@ -149,6 +149,18 @@ static void cpu_max_set_sve_max_vq(Object *obj, Visitor *v, const char *name,
     cpu->sve_max_vq = max_vq;
 }
 
+static bool cpu_max_get_dic(Object *obj, Error **errp)
+{
+    ARMCPU *cpu = ARM_CPU(obj);
+    return FIELD_EX64(cpu->ctr, CTR_EL0, DIC);
+}
+
+static void cpu_max_set_dic(Object *obj, bool value, Error **errp)
+{
+    ARMCPU *cpu = ARM_CPU(obj);
+    cpu->ctr = FIELD_DP64(cpu->ctr, CTR_EL0, DIC, value);
+}
+
 static bool cpu_arm_get_rme(Object *obj, Error **errp)
 {
     ARMCPU *cpu = ARM_CPU(obj);
@@ -1389,6 +1401,7 @@ void aarch64_max_tcg_initfn(Object *obj)
     aarch64_add_sme_properties(obj);
     object_property_add(obj, "sve-max-vq", "uint32", cpu_max_get_sve_max_vq,
                         cpu_max_set_sve_max_vq, NULL, NULL);
+    object_property_add_bool(obj, "dic", cpu_max_get_dic, cpu_max_set_dic);
     object_property_add_bool(obj, "x-rme", cpu_arm_get_rme, cpu_arm_set_rme);
     object_property_add(obj, "x-l0gptsz", "uint32", cpu_max_get_l0gptsz,
                         cpu_max_set_l0gptsz, NULL, NULL);
